WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.402
-Hey, Senator Sanders.
You look great.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:04.570
Really good to see you again.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.672
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.007
-Thanks for having me, Jimmy.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:09.775
-There's a lot to talk about.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:13.546
First, I'd love to get your
thoughts on last night's debate.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.815
-Well, what I think is that

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:19.252
it was certainly not as crazy
a debate as the first debate.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.889
-Yeah.
-But I continue to be astounded

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.691
by the degree
to which Donald Trump lies --

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.760
just lies and lies and lies --

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.395
not only his lies,

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:34.633
his downplaying of this
terrible pandemic from Day One

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.469
is just astounding to me.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:39.839
And I hope the American people
understand that

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.408
because of his irresponsibility,

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.443
because of his rejection
of science,

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:47.080
his attacks on Dr. Fauci,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.517
that tens of thousands of people
have died unnecessarily.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.254
-One of the things
I admired about you

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.822
is that you endorsed
Vice President Biden,

00:00:56.822 --> 00:01:00.527
although you don't agree
with him on every issue.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:04.430
I just think that sends a --

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.833
what -- what message
are you sending there?

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:10.169
-Well, the message is that --
let me be very frank --

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:11.737
and not everybody
will agree with me,

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:15.708
but I think that Donald Trump
is the most dangerous president

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.443
in the modern history
of this country,

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:20.112
and it's not just because
he lies all the time.

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:22.815
It's not just because
he doesn't believe in science.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.149
It's not just because

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:28.354
he's a racist or a sexist
or a homophobe or a xenophobe,

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:31.190
it is because
he is quite intentionally

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.860
trying to undermine
American democracy,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.261
trying to suppress the vote.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.297
We are a democratic society.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:41.401
People have fought and died
to defend our democracy,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.836
and we cannot re-elect
the president

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.339
who does not believe
in the rule of law,

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:50.009
our Constitution,
or, in fact, our democracy.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.145
I have known Joe
for many, many years.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.047
He is a very decent guy.
As you have indicated,

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:58.851
he and I have differences of
opinions on a number of issues.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.220
But I can vouch for his decency

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.790
and his belief in the rule
of law and democracy.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.459
-When was the first time --
do you remember

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.961
meeting Joe Biden,
Vice President?

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:11.664
-Oh, I do. You know, he was
a senator, and I was a senator.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.432
He was around
for a very long time.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:14.633
I was new.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:15.768
And the thing I think

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.437
that people will learn
bout Joe Biden --

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.106
he is a very, very
down-to-earth guy.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:23.543
My wife remembers the first time
that she met him,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.678
and she never, you know,
talked to him at all.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.748
He sat down, and he chatted
with her about Ireland --

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.783
their families
both come from Ireland.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:34.853
-Yeah.
-Very -- Very human guy.

00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:36.655
A very empathetic guy.

00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:39.825
-Although the election
is November 3rd,

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.561
and it's been said that
we won't know the results

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.363
until days later,

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.633
when do you think
we'll know the results?

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.468
-Jimmy, you raise
an important point,

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:51.738
and I hope the American
people understand it,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:54.707
because this is something
I worry about.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:58.778
My view is every vote
must be counted.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.815
For reasons which I don't have
the time to get into tonight,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.985
you're going to have
a situation, I suspect,

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:10.956
in states like Pennsylvania,
Michigan, Wisconsin,

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:12.358
other states,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.761
where they
are going to be receiving

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:17.963
huge amounts of mail-in ballots.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:20.967
And unlike states
like Florida or Vermont,

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:24.437
they're not able,
for bad reasons,

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:28.474
to begin processing
those ballots until --

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.644
I don't know -- Election Day
or maybe when the polls close.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.179
That means
you're going to have states

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:37.049
dealing with perhaps millions
of mail-in ballots.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:39.118
Here is my worry.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.853
What polls show,

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:44.256
and what studies have shown
is that, for whatever reason,

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:48.594
Democrats are more likely
to use mail-in ballots.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:52.298
Republicans are more likely
to walk into polling booths

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.933
on Election Day.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:57.570
It is likely that the first
votes that will be counted

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.006
will be those people
who came in on Election Day,

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:02.475
which will be Republican.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.743
And here is the fear --

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.445
and I hope everybody hears it --

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.012
it could well be --
you know,

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:09.282
I don't know what's going to
happen -- nobody does.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:13.152
But it could well be that,
at 10:00 on election night,

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:17.423
Trump is winning in Michigan,
he's winning in Pennsylvania,

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.991
he's winning in Wisconsin,

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:21.127
and he gets on the television
and he says,

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.762
"Thank you, Americans,
for re-electing me.

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:26.332
It's all over.
Have a good day."

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.335
But then, the next day
and the day following,

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:32.438
all of those mail-in ballots
start getting counted,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:35.240
and it turns out that Biden
has won those states.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.576
At which point Trump says,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:39.846
"See? I told whole thing
was fraudulent.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:43.448
I told you those mail-in ballots
were crooked.

00:04:43.448 --> 00:04:46.685
And I got -- you know, we're not
going to leave office."

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.889
So that is a worry
that I and a lot of people have.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.625
So, the results -- you know,
we don't know what's happened.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:53.860
-Sure.
-Maybe the results will be known

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.127
on election night.

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:59.465
But people should be aware
of that possibility.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.535
-I know that
you have been working

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:06.939
with people running in Texas.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.707
Why is Texas important now?

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:12.912
I feel like a lot of people
are highlighting Texas.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:18.684
-I think that Texas may be --
in many ways,

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:22.855
Texas is the future of
progressive politics in America.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:27.893
Historically, because there has
been a lot of voter suppression,

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:29.395
Texas is one of the states

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.631
where their Republican
state government has,

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.132
for a long time,

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:36.736
tried to make it as difficult
as possible for people to vote.

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:39.105
But you have folks over there --
Beto O'Rourke and others

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:41.774
are doing a great job
registering people,

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.075
getting people to vote.

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:49.248
The bottom line is that if Texas
becomes a blue state

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.951
and a progressive state,
as I think it can --

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.386
it has a lot of young people.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:56.522
It has a lot of Latinos,
a lot of African-Americans.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.791
It can become
a progressive state.

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.158
And if that happens,

00:06:00.158 --> 00:06:04.029
and if those 38 electoral votes
go Democratic,

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:06.732
then we've changed the face
of American politics.

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:09.235
-Wow.
I think that would be --

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.737
that would be -- I mean,
are people predicting that?

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:14.006
Or this is just your people?

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.408
-There's no question
the trend is with us.

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:20.546
What we don't know is how
it plays out this election.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.948
And to those people out there
who say,

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:25.050
"Oh, Texas is
a conservative state" --

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.953
trust me, it is not.

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:31.057
You have some great,
great progressive candidates

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:34.960
who are running for office
who stand a great chance to win,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.230
and the future is with
progressive politics in Texas.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.799
-It will be interesting to watch
what happens in Texas.

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:44.503
Bernie Sanders, thank you so
much for coming back to my show.

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:47.806
And give my best
to the grandkids.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:49.875
I know we always talk about them
every time you're on.

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:52.644
And, God, you always smile
every time I bring them up.

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.647
But I appreciate you
coming back on the show.

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:56.315
It means a lot to me,
so thank you.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.583
Senator Bernie Sanders,
everyone.

